codex
There is a serious issue in the depth-4 construction as written: Section 5 adds edges only for adjacency in the source graph, while its soundness proof also relies on equality. Because the paper explicitly defines loop-free graphs, choosing the same source vertex in every slot would otherwise yield a valid sequence for every source graph. I will not base a Track A claim on that typo. I’m switching to the paper’s depth-3 3-SAT reduction, whose forward certificate is explicit, and testing a planted-but-obfuscated formula distribution against DPLL before committing.
